A||||4||Hym-The-Man||See what you think||||1||
Z||000000||Hym-The-Man||02-04-2001||05:00 PM||||I am going to do a Northstar conversion here is how it will be done<P>I understand that the swap will be difficult. I think that I have all of the bases covered. See what you guys think.<P>According to Composite Exotic Tech. The engine cradle from a v6 Fiero is almost a perfect match for either a N* or Aurora v8, check it out: <A HREF="http://www.compositeeti.com/FAQ.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.compositeeti.com/FAQ.htm</A> <P>Suspension will be handled by:  <A HREF="http://www.shelbycustom.com/addons/addons.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.shelbycustom.com/addons/addons.html</A>  <P>Brakes will be handled by:  <A HREF="http://www.ipass.net/~fieroman/terranexus//fieroman/walt/walt.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ipass.net/~fieroman/terranexus//fieroman/walt/walt.htm</A>  <P> Engine Management will be handled by:  <A HREF="http://www.chrfab.com/Ignitions.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.chrfab.com/Ignitions.htm</A>  <P>Shifting will be handled by an Aurora standard tranny or modified Getrag, although I wish that I could find a<BR>6-speed tranny for the thing.<P>Bigger radiator, Higher volume fuel pump, Larger master cylinder, Mr. Mikes Leather seat covers style 430,Seat heaters for cold winter days by: <A HREF="http://home.flash.net/~duetto/general/genseatheaters.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home.flash.net/~duetto/general/genseatheaters.htm</A>  <P>I am also going to have the heads ported and polished by chrfab for an extra 20 Hp. My friend works in a muffler shop so I have the exhaust covered.<P>I am also going to reinforce the chasis first of all to add alittle weight to the front and to strengthen it overall.<P>I am wishing that someone had information on doing a anti-lock brake conversion.<P><BR>So what do you think? Let me know what suggeston you guys have.<P>                ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||02-05-2001||12:13 AM||||Good luck.  BTW--Mr. Mikes sells seat heaters.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Got2manyfieros||02-05-2001||01:33 PM||||I believe that quaif might sell a FWD 6 Speed, but I'm not sure that would be compatible with the fiero setup.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||02-05-2001||02:34 PM||||Personaly, Id stay away from any anti-lock. Only thing ive ever seen good about them is in tv tests or commercials. I know lots of friends (mostly vette owners) who pull the electic plug to disable them. In performance driving, I like unassisted brakes, with high pedal pressure. Lot harder to lock them up, and if you notice no one races with them that I know of, SCCA, NASCAR, ASA, ETC.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Hym-The-Man||02-05-2001||06:06 PM||||Good point about the race cars and anti-lock brakes, but I am thinking about general safety.  I can personally vouch for the fact that abs has saved my life on more than one occasion.  I think that it will be hard to adapt, but I am willing to put in the work.<P>Anyone know where I can find a wrecked caddi with a northstar in good shape?||||reg||1
